      given: "It settled the Iraq-Turkey dispute over Mosul in 1926 and the Colombia-Peru border dispute in the early 1930s, but failed to stop the Italian invasion of Ethiopia, the Spanish Civil War and the Second Sino-Japanese War.",
      formula: "Historical concept: an organization can succeed in small disputes yet fail in major conflicts when great powers do not support it.",
      substitution: "Its successes were limited disputes; its failures involved aggression by powerful states, including a permanent Council member, Italy.",
