      given: "After the crash of October 1929 consumer spending and investment dropped, industrial output declined and crop prices fell by about 60 percent.",
      formula: "Historical concept: modern economies are linked, so a crisis in one sector spreads to others.",
      substitution: "Factories laid off workers, workers bought less, demand for farm produce fell, so farm prices and incomes collapsed.",
      calculation: "The fall in prices and jobs spread from the city to the countryside, so rural communities suffered too.",
      answer: "The crash destroyed demand and jobs in the cities, which reduced the demand for farm produce and cut farm prices."
