  simple: "The Second World War was fought from 1939 to 1945 between the Allied Powers, mainly France, Britain, the USA and the USSR, and the Axis Powers of Germany, Japan and Italy. Its causes included fascist aggression in Germany, Italy and Japan, the effects of the Great Depression, and the failure of Britain and France to stop aggression through appeasement while the USA stayed isolated. Germany invaded Poland on 1 September 1939, and Britain and France declared war on 3 September. The Allies won decisive victories at Stalingrad and Kursk, opened a second front in 1944, and entered Berlin in 1945. Hitler killed himself, Germany surrendered, atomic bombs fell on Hiroshima and Nagasaki, and Japan surrendered on 2 September 1945.",
  detailed: "<p><b>The two blocs.</b> The Second World War was fought between two major military blocs, the Allied and the Axis Powers, from 1939 to 1945. The Allied Powers consisted mainly of France, Britain, the USA, which joined in December 1941, and the USSR, while the Axis Powers were made up of Germany, Japan and Italy, which joined after June 1940.</p><p><b>Causes: fascist aggression.</b> One major cause was the ascendancy of the fascists in Germany, Italy and Japan. The German Nazis complained that the Treaty of Versailles was a dictated peace and that Germany had been treated unfairly, so the desire to restore Germany's old position drove them to revenge and aggression. Italy under the Fascist Party subscribed to national chauvinism and Mussolini aspired to build a great Italian empire in Africa, while militaristic Japan planned to expand its empire by conquest.</p><p><b>Causes: depression, appeasement and isolation.</b> The Great Depression created economic troubles and political instability in many countries, and leaders such as Hitler, Mussolini and the Japanese military cliques promised a better future and embarked on aggression. The Western powers failed to create a united front against Fascist aggression: Britain and France followed a policy of appeasement, prepared to allow territorial seizures to avoid another war, while the USA adopted a policy of isolation. This encouraged the Fascist states to intensify their conquests.</p><p><b>Aggression before the war.</b> In 1931 Japan invaded Manchuria, a northern province of China, and when the League condemned it Japan withdrew from the League in May 1933; in 1937 Japan began the Sino-Japanese War for the total subjugation of China. Germany rearmed against the disarmament clauses of Versailles and withdrew from the League in October 1933, and it reoccupied the Rhineland in March 1936. Fascist Italy invaded Ethiopia in October 1935, and the Spanish Civil War of 1936-39 saw Germany and Italy intervene while General Franco overthrew the republican government. In March 1938 Hitler incorporated Austria in the Anschluss, and in September 1938 Britain, France and Germany signed the Munich agreement allowing Germany to occupy the Sudeten part of Czechoslovakia, which Hitler annexed in March 1939.</p><p><b>Course: the war begins.</b> In August 1939 Germany and the USSR signed the Nazi-Soviet Non-aggression Pact. Germany invaded Poland on 1 September 1939, which marked the beginning of the war, and on 3 September 1939 Britain and France declared war on Germany. Poland was overrun within three weeks in a campaign the Germans called Blitzkrieg, or lightning war; Germany annexed western Poland while Russia invaded the eastern provinces and annexed Estonia, Latvia, Lithuania and Finland. In May 1940 Germany invaded France through neutral Holland and Belgium, bypassing the Maginot Line, defeated the Allied force and occupied over half of France. In unoccupied France the Nazis formed a puppet government under Marshal Petain at Vichy, while General Charles de Gaulle formed a French Free government in England. Hitler's air attacks on Britain were repulsed by effective British resistance.</p><p><b>Course: the turning of the tide.</b> Despite the pact, the Nazis invaded Russia in June 1941, but the Soviets resisted and communist guerrillas harassed the invaders. When Japan attacked the US naval base at Pearl Harbor in Hawaii in December 1941, the USA declared war on Japan, and Germany and Italy declared war on the USA, so America entered the war. In 1942 the Axis powers were at their height, but the Soviet victories at Stalingrad in 1942-43 and Kursk in 1943 were decisive and began the Allied counter-offensive. In May 1943 Britain, France and the USA drove German and Italian forces out of North Africa, and in 1944 the Allies opened a second front in Europe.</p><p><b>Course: victory and effects.</b> The 1943 Allied invasion of Italy hastened Mussolini's overthrow, France was liberated in 1944, and by June 1944 Allied forces had overrun much of Italy. Russia entered Berlin, Hitler committed suicide on 30 April 1945, Mussolini was murdered in 1945, and Germany surrendered unconditionally. In the Pacific, the USA dropped atomic bombs on Hiroshima and Nagasaki on 6 and 9 August 1945, US forces occupied Tokyo, and Japan surrendered unconditionally on 2 September 1945. The war cost about 50 million lives, hastened decolonization in Asia and Africa, made the USA and the USSR superpowers, began the Cold War and gave birth to the United Nations Organization, which replaced the League of Nations.</p>",
